.TH CTBREC-VR 1 "2026-10-10" "ctbrec-vr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-vr \- move finished VR ctbrec recordings into the VR destination folder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-vr
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-vr
scans a ctbrec recordings tree (default
.IR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec ),
identifies recordings whose first video stream is larger than 1080p, and
renames those that are no longer being written into the destination
directory. The destination defaults to
.IR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/vr
for the default recordings root, and to a
.B vr
subfolder of
.B \-\-dir
for any other root; it can always be overridden with
.BR \-\-dest .
.P
A recording is considered VR when its video height is greater than
.B \-\-base\-height
(default 1080) or its width is greater than
.B \-\-base\-width
(default 1920). At this site that captures the stereoscopic 5760\(mu2880,
4096\(mu2048 and related formats while excluding every regular 1080p/720p
stream, and it does not rely on model names (which can contain
.RB \(lq vr \(rq
without being VR).
.P
A recording is considered finished when it is neither open for writing
(inode\-based
.B /proc
file\-descriptor check, so recorders in an LXC container are detected) nor
modified within
.B \-\-age
seconds (default 900).
.P
Moves use
.BR rename (2)
within the same filesystem, so they are instant, copy no data, and need no
extra space. Files already known to be non\-VR are remembered in a small cache
so that repeated runs probe only genuinely new recordings; a steady\-state run
therefore does almost no work. The scan covers the recordings root and one
level of per\-model subdirectories, skipping
.IR vr ,
.IR .merged_originals ,
.IR compressing ,
and hidden directories.
.P
Probes run
.B ffprobe
under
.BR nice (1)
and
.BR ionice (1)
class 3 by default, and the whole run is
.I deferred
(not queued) when host I/O pressure is above
.B \-\-io\-threshold .
.P
The script runs as root, but the recordings share is managed over Samba as
another user. Because deleting a file needs write permission on its
directory, the destination is chowned and chmodded on every run to match the
recordings root (or the explicit
.BR \-\-owner / \-\-group / \-\-dir\-mode ).
This also repairs a destination that an earlier run left root\-owned.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Recordings root to scan. Default:
.IR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec .
.TP
.BI \-\-dest " DIR"
Destination directory. Default:
.I /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/vr
for the default recordings root, otherwise
.IR DIR/vr .
.TP
.BI \-\-owner " USER"
Owner (name or uid) for the destination directory. Default: the owner of
.BR \-\-dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-group " GROUP"
Group (name or gid) for the destination directory. Default: the group of
.BR \-\-dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-dir\-mode " OCTAL"
Permission mode, in octal, for the destination directory. Default: the mode of
.BR \-\-dir
(here 0775).
.TP
.BI \-\-age " SECONDS"
Skip files modified within this many seconds. Default: 900.
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-height " PX"
Treat a recording as VR when its video height exceeds
.IR PX .
Default: 1080.
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-width " PX"
Treat a recording as VR when its video width exceeds
.IR PX .
Default: 1920.
.TP
.B \-\-top\-level
Only scan
.B \-\-dir
itself, never descend into per\-model subdirectories.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-moves " N"
Stop after
.I N
moves. Default 0 = unlimited.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " FILE"
Path to the non\-VR cache file. Default:
.IR /var/lib/ctbrec\-vr/nonvr.txt
(or
.I ~/.cache/ctbrec\-vr/nonvr.txt
when that is not writable).
.TP
.BI \-\-lock " FILE"
Lock file used to prevent overlapping runs. Default:
.IR /run/ctbrec\-vr.lock ,
falling back to
.IR /tmp/ctbrec\-vr.lock
when
.I /run
is not writable.
.TP
.BI \-\-io\-threshold " PCT"
Defer the run when host I/O pressure
.RB ( /proc/pressure/io ,
.B "full avg10" )
exceeds this percentage. Default: 40, which only trips under genuine
contention; normal recording load here sits around 3\(en9%.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-io\-check
Do not defer on I/O pressure.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-active
Skip the open\-for\-write check and rely on
.B \-\-age
alone.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-nice
Do not run
.B ffprobe
under
.BR nice (1)/ ionice (1).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would move; change nothing and do not update the cache.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Files considered
Files ending in
.B .ts
or
.B .mts
in the recordings root and in one level of subdirectories, excluding the
skipped directories listed above. Zero\-length files are ignored, and files
whose header cannot be probed are left in place and retried on a later run.
.SS Moving
A matching file is renamed into
.BR \-\-dest .
If a file of the same name already exists there, a numeric suffix is added.
.SS Scheduling
A systemd timer
.RI ( ctbrec\-vr.timer )
runs the script every 15 minutes with
.BR Nice=19
and
.BR IOSchedulingClass=idle .
.SS Requirements
.B ffprobe
from
.BR ffmpeg (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview what would move, changing nothing:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Run a normal pass over the default tree:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr
.EE
.P
Move files that are only 5 minutes old, ignoring I/O pressure:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr \-\-age 300 \-\-no\-io\-check
.EE
.P
Move at most 20 files this run:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-vr \-\-max\-moves 20
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, deferred on I/O pressure, or another run held the lock.
.TP
.B 1
Bad options, missing directory, or
.B ffprobe
unavailable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/ctbrec-vr/nonvr.txt
Cache of filenames already classified as non\-VR.
.TP
.I /run/ctbrec-vr.lock
Lock held for the duration of a run.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/ctbrec-vr.service
.TQ
.I /etc/systemd/system/ctbrec-vr.timer
Systemd units that drive the recurring run.
.TP
.I /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/vr
Default destination for moved recordings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-vr-remote (1),
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
